{"The domain-matching regex is not anchored to the end of the string, so an email whose domain merely contains an allowed/blocked domain as a prefix (e.g. 'user@allowed.com.evil.com') will incorrectly match, allowing whitelist bypasses": 0.7343411445617676, "The email uniqueness validation is case-sensitive, but the rest of the model treats emails as case-insensitive (e.g. `find_by_username_or_email` downcases before querying), allowing two accounts with the same email differing only by case": 0.43424198031425476, "The computed property for email validation depends on `rejectedEmails.@each`, which won't reliably trigger recomputation when items are added or removed from the array; the dependency should be on `rejectedEmails.[]` to observe array content changes": 0.7233422994613647, "The `BlockedEmail.should_block?` method returns `nil` when no matching record exists, but the spec asserts `be_false` which expects a literal `false` and will fail when the subject is `nil`": 0.7680568695068359}